// The in-game homestead as a designed, theoretically 100%-closed-loop self-sustaining
// system (v0.432). Numbers come from the closed-loop design pass (2026-06-13), grounded
// in docs/design/self-sufficiency.md: energy is Wh/day not nameplate W, water closure is
// about dry-season STORAGE, food is the weakest loop (towers give variety + vitamins but
// only ~6% of calories; field crops carry the bulk), nutrients close via compost + urine.
// Anyone can load the game, walk the home, read each machine's role, and open the Home
// page to see the four loops balance. Data-driven (infinite-of-X): edit here, no code.
//
// REARRANGED 2026-09-19 for the home redesign. Two things to know before editing:
//
//  1. `room` now carries the ZONE ID of the room the machine stands in, exactly as
//     data/blueprints/ship_structure.ron spells it ("room-kitchen", not "kitchen"). In
//     zone mode the renderer positions a machine from its ABSOLUTE world x/z and only
//     clamps it into the zone, so `room` is a label; making it match the zone id is what
//     lets a test check that every machine really is standing in the room it claims.
//  2. The machine SET is fixed by the `loops` block at the bottom, which states counts in
//     prose ("8 solar panels", "26 towers", "2 aquaponic fish tanks"). Move machines
//     freely; adding or removing one that carries a power / water / food / nutrient stat
//     makes that text a lie. Furniture and displays have no stats and are free.
//
// Where each screen is and why: docs/design/player-home.md.

